{"label":"US CPI, October","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/archives/cpi_11102026.htm"}]},"schema_version":2,"statement_highlights":{"banks":[{"attribution":"Source: Bank of England, excerpted","bank":"boe","checked_at":"2026-11-14T06:00:00Z","decision":"Raised 25 bp to 4.00%","detail":"Vote 8–1; one member preferred a 50 bp increase to 4.25% (the previous vote was 6–3 to hold). The Bank's pre-meeting Market Participants Survey median already expected 4.00%.","detail_url":"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy-summary-and-minutes/2026/november-2026","highlights":[{"new_en":"The Committee will adjust Bank Rate as necessary to ensure CPI inflation returns to the 2% target in the medium term.","old_en":"The Committee stands ready to act as necessary to ensure that CPI inflation remains on track to meet the 2% target in the medium term.","spans":[{"kind":"equal","text":"The Committee"},{"kind":"removed","text":"stands ready to act"},{"kind":"added","text":"will adjust Bank Rate"},{"kind":"equal","text":"as necessary to ensure"},{"kind":"removed","text":"that"},{"kind":"equal","text":"CPI inflation"},{"kind":"removed","text":"remains on track"},{"kind":"added","text":"returns"},{"kind":"equal","text":"to"},{"kind":"removed","text":"meet"},{"kind":"equal","text":"the 2% target in the medium term."}],"subtext":"“Stands ready to act” becomes “will adjust Bank Rate”, and “remains on track” becomes “returns to”: an admission that inflation is off course. Every coming meeting is live. A hawkish edit.","zh":null},{"new_en":"However, the degree of inflationary pressure in the pipeline is now sufficient to warrant an increase in Bank Rate.","old_en":"However, the risk of such effects, against which policy needs to lean, is greater the longer higher energy prices persist or are more volatile.","spans":[{"kind":"equal","text":"However, the"},{"kind":"removed","text":"risk of such effects, against which policy needs to lean, is greater the longer higher energy prices persist or are more volatile."},{"kind":"added","text":"degree of inflationary pressure in the pipeline is now sufficient to warrant an increase in Bank Rate."}],"subtext":"In September the Committee only warned that the risk grows the longer energy prices stay elevated. Now it says the pressure already in the pipeline is enough to justify an increase: from warning to action.","zh":null}],"name":"Bank of England","new_date":"2026-11-05","old_date":"2026-09-17","old_source_url":"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy-summary-and-minutes/2026/september-2026","page_url":null,"source_url":"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy-summary-and-minutes/2026/november-2026"},{"attribution":"Source: Federal Reserve","bank":"fed","checked_at":"2026-11-14T06:00:00Z","decision":"Held at 3.75%–4.00%","detail":"Vote 10–2; Cook and Hammack preferred a further 25 bp increase (the Committee had raised by 25 bp on 16 September).","detail_url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20261028a.htm","highlights":[{"new_en":"The accumulation of more information will help the Committee determine the policy stance appropriate to ensure a timely return of inflation to the Committee's 2 percent goal.","old_en":"Today's policy action will support a timelier return to the Committee's 2 percent goal.","spans":[{"kind":"removed","text":"Today's policy action will support a timelier return"},{"kind":"added","text":"The accumulation of more information will help the Committee determine the policy stance appropriate to ensure a timely return of inflation"},{"kind":"equal","text":"to the Committee's 2 percent goal."}],"subtext":"September said the increase itself would bring inflation back sooner; October waits for “more information”. That signals a pause, not an end to tightening: whether December moves depends on the inflation and jobs data by then.","zh":null},{"new_en":"Economic activity is expanding at a strong pace.","old_en":"Economic activity is expanding at a solid pace.","spans":[{"kind":"equal","text":"Economic activity is expanding at a"},{"kind":"removed","text":"solid"},{"kind":"added","text":"strong"},{"kind":"equal","text":"pace."}],"subtext":"The growth assessment was upgraded from “solid” to “strong”, so the pause is not about weaker activity. It is one word in the growth sentence: a hawkish detail of limited weight.","zh":null}],"name":"Federal Reserve","new_date":"2026-10-28","old_date":"2026-09-16","old_source_url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20260916a.htm","page_url":"https://heronatlas.com/en/central-banks/fed/2026-10-28/","source_url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20261028a.htm"},{"attribution":"Source: Reserve Bank of Australia 2026, excerpted (CC BY 4.0)","bank":"rba","checked_at":"2026-11-14T06:00:00Z","decision":"Raised 25 bp to 4.85%","detail":"Vote 6–3; three members preferred to leave the cash rate target at 4.60% (the 29 September decision to raise was unanimous).","detail_url":"https://www.rba.gov.au/media-releases/2026/mr-26-30.html","highlights":[{"new_en":"The Board will continue to do what it considers necessary to bring inflation sustainably back to target.","old_en":"The Board will continue to do what it considers necessary to bring inflation sustainably back to target, including increasing the cash rate target further if needed.","spans":[{"kind":"equal","text":"The Board will continue to do what it considers necessary to bring inflation sustainably back to"},{"kind":"removed","text":"target, including increasing the cash rate target further if needed."},{"kind":"added","text":"target."}],"subtext":"The Board raised the cash rate but dropped “including increasing the cash rate target further if needed”. With three votes for no change, agreement on further tightening is weakening. A dovish edit.","zh":null},{"new_en":"Inflation is now expected to remain above 3 per cent for the coming year and there is an increasing risk that higher inflation expectations will become embedded.","old_en":"The Board remains focused on ensuring that high inflation does not become embedded.","spans":[{"kind":"removed","text":"The Board remains focused on ensuring that high inflation does not"},{"kind":"added","text":"Inflation is now expected to remain above 3 per cent for the coming year and there is an increasing risk that higher inflation expectations will"},{"kind":"equal","text":"become embedded."}],"subtext":"The inflation assessment hardened: inflation is expected above 3 per cent for the coming year, with a growing risk that expectations become embedded. Dropping the pledge is not a promise to stop.","zh":null}],"name":"Reserve Bank of Australia","new_date":"2026-11-03","old_date":"2026-09-29","old_source_url":"https://www.rba.gov.au/media-releases/2026/mr-26-27.html","page_url":null,"source_url":"https://www.rba.gov.au/media-releases/2026/mr-26-30.html"},{"attribution":"Source: ECB, excerpted","bank":"ecb","checked_at":"2026-11-14T06:00:00Z","decision":"All three key rates unchanged (deposit facility 2.50%)","detail":"On hold after the 25 bp increase of 10 September; the statement gives no vote.","detail_url":"https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/pr/date/2026/html/ecb.mp261029~9a493adf17.en.html","highlights":[{"new_en":null,"old_en":"The conflict in the Middle East continues to generate inflation pressures, and inflation is set to remain well above target for an extended period.","spans":[{"kind":"removed","text":"The conflict in the Middle East continues to generate inflation pressures, and inflation is set to remain well above target for an extended period."}],"subtext":"The flat judgement that inflation would stay “well above target for an extended period” is gone, but the new statement still says the energy shock is likely to drive inflation up. A conclusion has become a risk warning, which leaves room to stay on hold.","zh":null},{"new_en":"While the full effects of the energy shock are still unfolding, underlying inflation has remained broadly stable so far and wages do not show a material response at this stage.","old_en":null,"spans":[{"kind":"added","text":"While the full effects of the energy shock are still unfolding, underlying inflation has remained broadly stable so far and wages do not show a material response at this stage."}],"subtext":"The new sentence says underlying inflation has been broadly stable “so far” and wages show no “material” response “at this stage”. That is the case for pausing now; both qualifiers leave the door open, and wage data are one input to watch at future meetings.","zh":null}],"name":"European Central Bank","new_date":"2026-10-29","old_date":"2026-09-10","old_source_url":"https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/pr/date/2026/html/ecb.mp260910~314e508016.en.html","page_url":"https://heronatlas.com/en/central-banks/ecb/2026-10-29/","source_url":"https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/pr/date/2026/html/ecb.mp261029~9a493adf17.en.html"}],"default_bank":"boe"}}
